(function(E){ const x = E["int-m2"] = E["int-m2"] || {units:{}}; x.units["int-cp-2"] = {"exit":{"id":"c-int-cp-2-x","course":"interview","unit":"int-cp-2","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"int-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"I am responsible for ___ every task on the team board.","options":["checking","check","to checking"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"checking: 'for' is a preposition, so the verb takes -ing. 'Check' and 'to checking' don't follow responsible for.","tr":"checking: 'for' bir edattır, bu yüzden fiil -ing alır. 'Check' ve 'to checking' responsible for'dan sonra gelmez.","fa":"checking درست است، چون for حرف اضافه است و فعل بعدش ing می‌گیرد. check و to checking بعد از responsible for نمی‌آیند."}},{"from":"int-4","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is proof of a strength?","options":["I am a natural leader, and I always give my best at work.","Last year I led a team of six and we finished two weeks early.","Everybody says I am very good, and my manager loves my work."],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'I led a team of six and we finished two weeks early' is proof with a number. 'Natural leader' and 'everybody says' are claims.","tr":"'I led a team of six and we finished two weeks early' sayılı bir kanıttır. 'Natural leader' ve 'everybody says' birer iddiadır.","fa":"«I led a team of six and we finished two weeks early» مدرکی با عدد است. natural leader و everybody says فقط ادعا هستند."}},{"from":"int-5","kind":"blank","prompt":"While I ___ for the client, the fire alarm went off.","options":["waited","was waiting","have waited"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"was waiting: 'while' plus a long background action takes the past continuous. 'Waited' loses the background, and 'have waited' links to now.","tr":"was waiting: 'while' ve uzun bir arka plan eylemi past continuous alır. 'Waited' arka planı kaybeder; 'have waited' şimdiye bağlar.","fa":"was waiting درست است، چون while با کار طولانی پس‌زمینه گذشته‌ی استمراری می‌خواهد. waited پس‌زمینه را از بین می‌برد و have waited به الان ربط دارد."}},{"from":"int-5","kind":"mcq","prompt":"In a STAR story, which part should be the longest?","options":["The situation","What you did","The name of the company"],"correct":1,"point":1,"why":{"en":"What you did: the Action shows your skill, so it gets the most time. The situation is only the setting, and the company name is one word.","tr":"Ne yaptığın: Eylem becerini gösterir, bu yüzden en çok zamanı o alır. Durum yalnızca ortamdır; şirket adı tek bir kelimedir.","fa":"کاری که خودت کردی؛ همین بخش مهارتت را نشان می‌دهد و بیشترین وقت را می‌گیرد. موقعیت فقط زمینه است و اسم شرکت یک کلمه است."}},{"from":"int-6","kind":"blank","prompt":"Sorry, my screen ___ at the moment.","options":["is not working","not working","don't work"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"is not working: a problem right now takes is not + -ing. 'Not working' has no verb, and 'don't work' doesn't agree with 'my screen'.","tr":"is not working: şu anki bir sorun is not + -ing alır. 'Not working'te fiil yoktur; 'don't work' 'my screen' ile uyuşmaz.","fa":"is not working درست است، چون مشکل همین الان is not و فعل ing‌دار می‌خواهد. not working فعل ندارد و don't work با my screen جور نیست."}},{"from":"int-6","kind":"mcq","prompt":"In a video interview, where should you look for your most important sentences?","options":["At your own picture","At your notes","At the camera"],"correct":2,"point":1,"why":{"en":"At the camera: to them, that is eye contact. Looking at your own picture or your notes looks like looking away.","tr":"Kameraya: onlar için göz teması budur. Kendi görüntüne ya da notlarına bakmak başka yere bakıyormuşsun gibi görünür.","fa":"به دوربین؛ از نظر آن‌ها تماس چشمی یعنی همین. نگاه کردن به تصویر خودت یا یادداشت‌ها یعنی نگاهت جای دیگری است."}},{"from":"int-3","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence shows you have researched the company?","options":["I read that you are opening a branch in Konya.","Your company is very famous.","I have always wanted to work in an office."],"correct":0,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'You are opening a branch in Konya' is a fact you could only know from research. 'Very famous' and 'an office' fit any company.","tr":"'You are opening a branch in Konya' ancak araştırmayla bilinebilecek bir bilgidir. 'Very famous' ve 'an office' her şirkete uyar.","fa":"«You are opening a branch in Konya» واقعیتی است که فقط با تحقیق می‌دانی. very famous و an office به هر شرکتی می‌خورد."}},{"from":"int-11","kind":"blank","prompt":"We have ten minutes left. Why ___ on the top two ideas?","options":["don't we vote","we don't vote","don't we voting"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"don't we vote: in 'Why don't we + verb?', don't comes before we and the verb is plain. 'We don't vote' keeps statement order; 'voting' needs no -ing here.","tr":"don't we vote: 'Why don't we + fiil?' yapısında don't, we'den önce gelir ve fiil yalındır. 'We don't vote' düz cümle sırasıdır; 'voting' burada -ing almaz.","fa":"don't we vote درست است، چون در Why don't we و فعل، don't قبل از we می‌آید و فعل ساده است. we don't vote ترتیب جمله‌ی خبری است و voting اینجا ‎-ing نمی‌خواهد."}}]},"writing":{"id":"c-int-cp-2-w","title":{"en":"One story, a new question","tr":"Bir hikâye, yeni bir soru","fa":"یک ماجرا، سؤالی تازه"},"course":"interview","unit":"int-cp-2","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","modelBy":"FEschool","portfolio":"int-final-3","prompt":{"en":"Take one story from your bank. Write it out in full as an answer to \"Tell me about a time you worked under pressure\" (80-110 words). Change the first sentence so it fits this question. Keep the Situation and Task short, and make the Action the longest part.","tr":"Bankandan bir hikâye al. Onu \"Tell me about a time you worked under pressure\" sorusunun cevabı olarak tam yaz (80-110 kelime). İlk cümleyi bu soruya uyacak şekilde değiştir. Situation ve Task kısa kalsın, en uzun kısım Action olsun.","fa":"یک ماجرا از بانکت انتخاب کن. آن را کامل به‌عنوان جواب «Tell me about a time you worked under pressure» بنویس (۸۰ تا ۱۱۰ کلمه). جمله‌ی اول را طوری عوض کن که با این سؤال جور شود. Situation و Task کوتاه باشند و Action طولانی‌ترین بخش باشد."},"model":"The most pressure I have felt at work was last May. Our payment system crashed during a big sale, and I was the tester on duty. My job was to find the problem fast. I checked the last three updates and found the faulty one in twenty minutes. I told the team what to remove, and while they were working, I wrote a short message for customers. Then I tested the system again before we opened it. In the end, we lost less than an hour of sales, and we now test every update before a sale.","frame":"The most pressure I have felt at work was ___. ___, and I ___. My job was to ___. I ___. I ___, and while ___, I ___. Then I ___. In the end, ___.","words":[{"word":"while"},{"word":"My job was"},{"word":"In the end"}],"minWords":80,"minSentences":6,"rubric":["Task done: a true story that answers this question, with a result","Organised: short situation and task, long action, clear result","Language: past continuous for the background, past simple for the steps","Tone: factual and modest; \"I\" for what you did"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: bu soruyu cevaplayan, sonucu olan gerçek bir hikâye","Düzen: kısa durum ve görev, uzun eylem, net sonuç","Dil: arka plan için past continuous, adımlar için past simple","Üslup: gerçekçi ve alçakgönüllü; yaptıkların için \"I\""],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: ماجرایی واقعی که جواب این سؤال است و نتیجه دارد","نظم: موقعیت و وظیفه‌ی کوتاه، شرح طولانی کارهایت، نتیجه‌ی روشن","زبان: گذشته‌ی استمراری برای زمینه، گذشته‌ی ساده برای قدم‌ها","لحن: واقع‌گرا و فروتن؛ «I» برای کاری که خودت کردی"]},"parts":[{"t":{"en":"A first sentence that fits the question","tr":"Soruya uyan bir ilk cümle","fa":"جمله‌ی اولی که به سؤال می‌خورد"},"find":["the most pressure","pressure","a time when"],"sample":"the most pressure I have felt was last May"},{"t":{"en":"Situation and task, short","tr":"Durum ve görev, kısaca","fa":"موقعیت و وظیفه، کوتاه"},"find":["on duty","my job was","i was the","i was on"],"sample":"payment system crashed in a sale · I was the tester on duty"},{"t":{"en":"Your actions, with I","tr":"I ile anlattığın eylemler","fa":"کارهایی که کردی، با ⁨I⁩"},"find":["i checked","i told","i wrote","i called","i found","then i"],"sample":"checked 3 updates · told the team · wrote to customers"},{"t":{"en":"The result","tr":"Sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"},"find":["in the end","as a result","we lost","result"],"sample":"under an hour of sales lost · now we test every update"}]},"speaking":{"id":"int-cp-2","course":"interview","unit":"int-cp-2","topic":{"en":"A recorded round","tr":"Kayıt turu","fa":"یک دور ضبط"},"warmup":{"en":"Treat this as a recorded interview. Put your phone at eye level, press record and test your sound: \"Can you hear me okay?\" Nobody will see this but you.","tr":"Bunu kayıtlı bir mülakat gibi düşün. Telefonunu göz hizasına koy, kaydı başlat ve sesini dene: \"Can you hear me okay?\" Bunu senden başka kimse görmeyecek.","fa":"این را یک مصاحبه‌ی ضبط‌شده در نظر بگیر. گوشی‌ات را هم‌سطح چشمت بگذار، ضبط را بزن و صدایت را امتحان کن: «Can you hear me okay?» این را کسی جز خودت نمی‌بیند."},"questions":[{"en":"For each question: read it, think for 30 seconds, answer in 90 seconds. \"What is your greatest strength?\"","tr":"Her soru için: oku, 30 saniye düşün, 90 saniyede cevap ver. \"What is your greatest strength?\"","fa":"هر سؤال را بخوان، ۳۰ ثانیه فکر کن و در ۹۰ ثانیه جواب بده. «What is your greatest strength?»"},{"en":"\"What is your biggest weakness?\"","tr":"\"What is your biggest weakness?\"","fa":"«What is your biggest weakness?»"},{"en":"\"Tell me about a time you made a mistake at work.\"","tr":"\"Tell me about a time you made a mistake at work.\"","fa":"«Tell me about a time you made a mistake at work.»"}],"followups":[{"en":"Watch your recording once and tick the checklist. Then answer your weakest question again in 60 seconds, then 45.","tr":"Kaydını bir kez izle ve kontrol listesini işaretle. Sonra en zayıf cevabını önce 60, sonra 45 saniyede yeniden söyle.","fa":"ضبطت را یک بار ببین و چک‌لیست را تیک بزن. بعد ضعیف‌ترین جوابت را دوباره اول در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه بگو."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"I'm good at + -ing","meaning":{"en":"Names a skill, not an adjective.","tr":"Bir sıfat değil, bir beceri söyler.","fa":"یک مهارت را می‌گوید، نه یک صفت."}},{"phrase":"My job was to...","meaning":{"en":"Gives the T in STAR.","tr":"STAR'daki T'yi verir.","fa":"همان T در STAR را می‌گوید."}},{"phrase":"What I changed after that was...","meaning":{"en":"Shows what you learned from a mistake.","tr":"Bir hatadan ne öğrendiğini gösterir.","fa":"نشان می‌دهد از یک اشتباه چه یاد گرفتی."}}],"model":"Last March, I was preparing a client report when I saw that I had sent the wrong figures the day before. My job was to fix it fast. I took responsibility, called the client myself, explained the mistake and sent the right report within an hour. The client thanked me for telling them first. What I changed after that was simple: now I always check the numbers twice.","selfCheck":[{"en":"I looked at the camera, not at my own picture.","tr":"Kendi görüntüme değil, kameraya baktım.","fa":"به دوربین نگاه کردم، نه به تصویر خودم."},{"en":"My strength had a real moment as proof.","tr":"Güçlü yönümde kanıt olarak gerçek bir an vardı.","fa":"نقطه‌ی قوتم یک موقعیت واقعی به‌عنوان شاهد داشت."},{"en":"My mistake was real, and I said what I changed.","tr":"Hatam gerçekti ve neyi değiştirdiğimi söyledim.","fa":"اشتباهم واقعی بود و گفتم چه چیزی را عوض کردم."},{"en":"Each answer ended before 90 seconds.","tr":"Her cevap 90 saniyeden önce bitti.","fa":"هر جواب قبل از ۹۰ ثانیه تمام شد."}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
